  "limitations": [
    "Lifecycle and selection semantics are modeled in host tests and traced statically; this report does not claim on-device startup behavior or timing.",
    "If Japanese is not enabled/configured or its packs are not ready when startup selects, native behavior is retained; there is no delayed override that could undo a manual switch.",
    "An active restarting=true callback does not force Japanese. A new nonrestarting callback is treated as a new input session; a finish/hide followed by any startup is fresh.",
    "Manual-switch preservation refers to the selected language and to ordinary continued typing. On an active onStartInputView restart, the original g0.b already resets ABC_SECONDARY (q=true) to primary (q=false), even when no JapaneseStart selection occurs. This patch leaves that existing native mode reset intact; it does not promise to preserve every secondary Latin mode across a framework restart.",
    "Host tests also cover repeated restarting=true callbacks before the first native selection, preserving the unconsumed start marker. This is a modeled reentry boundary, not an observed on-device callback sequence."
  ],
